  "text_md": "# RESEARCH PAPER\n\n276 Karim et al. / Food Research 8 (1) (2024) 273 - 280\n\nTable 4. Intestinal microbiota test results of the control group (CG).\n\nMean (log DNA copies/g) ± SD Δ Average % p Value*\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Microbiota Pre-Test (D-0)<br><br>Post Test I (D-35)<br><br>Post Test II (D-42)</th>\n    <th>Day 0 and 35 Day 35 and 42 Day 0 and 35 Day 35 and 42</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Bifidobacterium 4.79±0.37 4.81±0.31 4.77±0.51</td>\n    <td>↑0.5% ↓0.8% 0.8 0.84</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Bacteroides 0.00±0.00 3.03±1.50 2.45±0.44</td>\n    <td>↑3.0% ↓19% 0.043 0.345</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Clostridium 6.73±0.46 6.59±0.60 6.60±0.56</td>\n    <td>↓2% ↑0.1% 0.432 0.822</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Lactobacillus 6.79±0.54 6.83±0.57 6.85±0.30</td>\n    <td>↑0.6% ↑0.3% 0.884 0.914</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>E. coli 5.48±1.22 5.63±2.30 5.48±1.97</td>\n    <td>↑2.8% ↓2.7% 0.774 0.38</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nCG: Control Group – standard feed only\n\n*p<0.05 significantly different.\n\nTable 5. Intestinal microbiota statistics test results treatment group I.\n\nMean (log DNA copies/g) ± SD Δ Average % p Value*\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Microbiota Pre-Test (D-0)<br><br>Post Test I (D-35)<br><br>Post Test II (D-42)</th>\n    <th>Day 0 and 35 Day 35 and 42 Day 0 and 35 Day 35 and 42</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Bifidobacterium 5.36±0.53 4.15±0.22 4.20±0.27</td>\n    <td>↓22.5% ↑1.2% 0.003 0.665</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Bacteroides 0.53±0.73 0.00±0.00 0.00±0.00</td>\n    <td>↓100% 0% 0.180 1.000</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Clostridium 6.17±0.81 7.40±0.32 7.74±0.17</td>\n    <td>↑19.9% ↑4.6% 0.013 0.095</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Lactobacillus 6.89±0.71 7.83±0.25 7.64±0.54</td>\n    <td>↑13.7% ↓2.5% 0.034 0.480</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>E. coli 3.71±1.24 6.91±2.56 6.54±2.70</td>\n    <td>↑86.4% ↓5.4% 0.043 0.138</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\n- TG I: Treatment Group I — standard feed and HFD intervention